-- DB update 2026_09_05_32 -> 2026_09_05_33
--
-- Shape-based itemization (docs/itemization-phase-2.md), implementation order step 9 follow-up,
-- REVISED: item_weapon_dps_curve refit against Str/Agi (melee/physical) weapons only, AND split
-- by hand category -- new `is_single_slot` column, part of the primary key.
--
-- The existing curve (itemization-changes.md §9.4) pooled EVERY live Rare/Epic weapon into one
-- median per (ilvl, quality) cell, caster weapons included. That's the wrong sample: real
-- Blizzard caster staves/wands are itemized with deliberately weak DPS since casters don't use
-- it directly (§7.7's whole point -- "a caster staff and a warrior staff... receive identical
-- DPS... the caster item is strictly worse"), so pooling them in drags the melee baseline down
-- below what a str/agi weapon's DPS should actually be. Refit from a real (entry <= 56806)
-- weapon sample restricted to items with a Str/Agi/AttackPower stat and NO Int/Spirit/SpellPower
-- stat -- 1,048 unambiguous physical weapons (Quality Rare/Epic, real dmg/delay data) out of
-- 2,463 total real weapons with usable DPS data.
--
-- The `is_single_slot` split is a second, independent fix, added after the first version of this
-- refit went out still pooling One-Hand together with Two-Hand/Ranged/Thrown/Relic. Real
-- single-slot weapons (no off-hand/shield to also carry stats) run consistently ~1.30x a
-- paired-slot weapon's DPS at the same ilvl/quality -- confirmed flat across the whole real ilvl
-- range, a deliberate WotLK itemization constant, not noise. Pooling them made every real
-- Two-Hand/Ranged/Thrown weapon look "above curve" (large positive dps_delta) and every real
-- One-Hand weapon look "at or below curve" -- with item_weapon_dps_cost = 7.0, that positive
-- delta on a Two-Hand weapon routinely cost more budget than the item had to spend, clamping
-- effective_budget to 0 and zeroing every stat on the item (confirmed: entries 7723 "Mograine's
-- Might", 9413 "The Rockpounder", 11921 "Impervious Giant", all Two-Hand maces -- 317 of 651
-- assigned Two-Hand weapons hit this wall overall, alongside most Thrown and some Ranged, while
-- 0 of the One-Hand/Main Hand/Off Hand weapons ever did).
--
-- Same derivation method as before, run separately per category: median DPS per (ItemLevel,
-- Quality) cell (avg(dmg_min1, dmg_max1) / (delay/1000)), sample-size-weighted isotonic
-- regression (PAVA) per quality line, linear interpolation/extrapolation to ilvl 1-300. Real data:
-- paired Rare ilvl 18-200 (187 items) / Epic ilvl 56-284 (337 items); single Rare ilvl 20-200
-- (190 items) / Epic ilvl 48-284 (332 items); flat past each quality's own range, same convention
-- as every other curve in this system.
--
-- Schema change: `is_single_slot` (0=paired, 1=single) added to item_weapon_dps_curve, part of
-- its primary key. UNLIKE the rest of this session's tables, item_weapon_dps_curve is NOT new --
-- it (and item_budget_curve, item_stat_cost, item_slot_mult, and everything else this whole
-- percentage-allocation foundation depends on) is already live, serving the currently-running
-- OLD system right now (confirmed by direct query: live `acore_world` has 600 rows in this table
-- today, `item_itemization` does not exist there at all yet). The Phase-1 file in this same
-- directory has its CREATE TABLE updated to the new 3-column-PK schema too, but that's a
-- fresh-install convenience only (`IF NOT EXISTS` is a no-op against the already-existing live
-- table) -- the actual live-upgrade path is the ALTER below, which must run before the
-- DELETE/INSERT that follows it.
--
-- *** This file is consequently NO LONGER "schema-safe to apply standalone" the way its first
-- version was. The OLD, still-live ItemBudget.cpp queries this table with a bare `WHERE ilvl=?
-- AND quality=?` (no is_single_slot filter) expecting exactly one row back; against the new
-- 3-column-PK schema that query would match TWO rows (paired and single) and silently pick
-- whichever one the query planner returns first -- correct behavior requires the rewritten
-- ItemBudget.cpp (this session's C++ changes) to be built and deployed in the same restart. Hold
-- this file with the rest of the item_itemization/shape batch; do not apply alone. ***
--
ALTER TABLE `item_weapon_dps_curve`
  ADD COLUMN `is_single_slot` tinyint(1) unsigned NOT NULL DEFAULT '0'
    COMMENT '0=paired (One-Hand/Main Hand/Off Hand), 1=single-slot (Two-Hand/Ranged/Thrown/Relic)'
    AFTER `quality`,
  DROP PRIMARY KEY, ADD PRIMARY KEY (`ilvl`, `quality`, `is_single_slot`);
--
-- Because 1,764+ items already carry a nonzero dps_delta against the OLD (pooled, un-split)
-- curve, applying this before those deltas are recomputed (see the per-item follow-up migration,
-- same timestamp batch) would make their final DPS wrong relative to their own original items --
-- apply together, same sequencing constraint as the first version of this file had.
--
DELETE FROM `item_weapon_dps_curve` WHERE `quality` IN (3, 4);
